## 3) Why the new host still times out

`oodac/main.oo` import graph (python walk of `import "…"`): **150** modules,
21 717 lines, 856 982 source bytes. `np > 12` → modular loop.

`check_mod.oo` (WT +38 vs HEAD 52cc4b5) first loop: for each path,
`scan_fn_names(strip_import_lines(raw))`. `scan_fn_names` **tokenizes the
whole file** just to pick `fn IDENT` names, then `names_to_depth0_binds`,
then a **second** loop `run_check_core_binds` (lex + tokenize **again** +
secret + typecheck). Comment in `check_collect.oo` already says full
per-module TC with shared sig tables is **not** wired.

Live stack on the 120s `check oodac/main.oo` at t=58s (RSS 854 MB, 98% CPU,
0 voluntary ctx — no I/O wait):

```
oo_str_release
oo_slist_release
collect_tokens
tokenize_lines
scan_fn_names
run_check_path
main
```

Still in the **name-scan** tokenize, not `load_source_with_imports` concat.
RSS grew 0.58 → 0.85 → 1.24 → 1.46 → 1.58 → **1.82 GiB** at t=110s, then
timeout 120 killed it. **0 bytes** stdout/stderr (never reached `println("OK")`
and never a type ERR). So 45s is not "almost"; even 2 minutes is not enough
on this ELF.

Contrast (same host, small graph → `np ≤ 12` concat path, **finishes**):

| Path | Wall | rc | Note |
|------|------|----|------|
| p7 tiny `main.oo` | <8s | 0 | smoke first rail |
| `oodac/check_mod.oo` | 0.866s | 1 | type `undefined variable 'tokenize_lines'` — **not hung** |
| `oodac/check_collect.oo` | 3.785s | 1 | type `undefined variable 'set_has'` — **not hung** |

Single-file type miss is expected (no import graph). Smoke would treat a
**finished** non-zero `main.oo` check as OK. We never get there.

